1 0 0 1 48 677 Tm (Five takeaways to remember about inspection rights, written requests, and follow-up. Use) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 664 Tm (them as a one-page briefing before you write or speak.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 651 Tm (* Start with procedure: Map notice, cure, hearing, and decision duties before debating the aesthetics of inspection rights, written requests, and follow-up.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 638 Tm (* Make the decision point explicit: Your appeal should answer what records to demand first with exhibits, not adjectives.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 625 Tm (* Compare options deliberately: Know whether you are closer to Governing docs, Violation file, or Financial ledger before you escalate.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 612 Tm (* Write one remedy sentence: Boards skim-state waive, reduce, re-notice, or reverse in a single line tied to inspection rights, written requests, and follow-up.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 599 Tm (* Keep escalation proportionate: Match collections risk and dollar amount to mediation, counsel, or court only after the packet is complete.) Tj
